cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the manuscript and the repository."
title: "NATRIX: An Auditable Feature-Admission and Promotion Protocol for Inline HTTP Attack Detection"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for an evaluation of NATRIX, a role-based inline HTTP
  attack-detection architecture. The package contains the feature-admission
  gates, the CPPP promotion protocol and TLA+ model, the P1/P2 evaluation
  protocol, lexical and character-CNN baselines, CRS replay results, the v3-D
  positive control, and the manuscript build pipeline. All reported results are
  from public labelled HTTP corpora; no production or shadow-mode traffic is
  included.
type: software
